($t$Scoparia dulcis$t$, $t$Scoparia dulcis$t$, $t$Plantaginaceae$t$, $t$Famiglia botanica: Plantaginaceae. Portamento: Annual/Perennial. Altezza massima indicativa: 0.8 m. Sweet Broom, Scoparia dulcis, is a tropical flowering herb growing up to 1 m tall with square stems and simple leaves. The white or pink flowers form singly or in clusters of two. Fruits are brown capsules containing brown seeds. It is considered a weed in many areas but used as medicinal herb for a wide range of uses including treatment for digestive problems, pulmonary conditions, fever, skin disorders, hypertension, hemorrhoids, diarrhea, dysentery, insect bites, anemia, albuminuria, diabetes, herpes, etc. Seed infusion can be drunk. The leaves are used to sweeten well water and for tea and young shoots can be consumed as vegetable. The bushy stems are used as temporary brooms. Fresh or dried plants reportedly kill fleas, lice, and intestinal worms. Plant can be grown from seeds.$t$, $j${"luce": "Pieno sole", "acqua": "Moderata", "terreno": "Tollera terreno: sabbioso/leggero, medio, argilloso/pesante"}$j$::jsonb, ARRAY[$t$Scheda in bozza, importata automaticamente da Plants For A Future (pfaf.org): dati non verificati manualmente, da controllare prima di considerarli affidabili$t$, $t$Nome comune (inglese, fonte PFAF): Sweet Broom, Licorice Weed, Vassourinha$t$, $t$Rischi segnalati dalla fonte (testo originale in inglese, non tradotto per non alterarne il significato): None known$t$], $j${"irrigazione": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "concimazione": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "potatura": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "npk": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}}$j$::jsonb, $j${"famiglia_botanica": "Plantaginaceae", "giorni_germinazione": null, "giorni_trapianto": null, "giorni_raccolta": null, "finestra_semina": [], "finestra_trapianto": []